@description ReaNotes: notes for the track, item or FX you touched last
@author aurnik
@version 1.0.0
@changelog
  Initial release
@provides
  [darwin] reaper_reanotes.dylib https://github.com/aurnik/ReaNotes/releases/download/v$version/$path
@link
  Source repository https://github.com/aurnik/ReaNotes
  Issue tracker https://github.com/aurnik/ReaNotes/issues
@about
  # ReaNotes

  A dockable notes window that shows the note for whatever you touched last:
  a track, a media item or a plug-in. Track notes are saved in the project.
  Item notes are saved on the item, so duplicates, copies and splits carry
  their own copy. FX notes are saved once per plug-in and show up in every
  project that uses it.

  Notes are markdown, styled as you type: headings, bold, italic, lists,
  code, quotes and links (Cmd+click to open).

  After installing, restart REAPER, then run the action **ReaNotes:
  Show/hide notes window** (or Extensions > ReaNotes). Right-click the
  header to dock or undock the window.

  Requirements: macOS 11 or newer, REAPER 7 or newer.
